From: Silt OS maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] dash: calculate integer length without floating point

Neva does not yet preserve an EL0 floating-point context, so all Silt base
programs are built with -mgeneral-regs-only. Keep the existing conservative
decimal length bound while expressing log10(2) as a scaled integer constant.

--- a/src/shell.h
+++ b/src/shell.h
@@ -100,5 +100,5 @@ static inline int max_int_length(int bytes)
  */
 static inline int max_int_length(int bytes)
 {
-	return (bytes * 8 - 1) * 0.30102999566398119521 + 14;
+	return ((bytes * 8 - 1) * 30103) / 100000 + 14;
 }
